    "title": "One database is not enough",
    "body": "The marketplace's database holds 5 TB and takes 30,000 order writes per second at peak. One server holds about 1 TB comfortably and takes about 5,000 writes per second safely. Read replicas (SD 6) do not help: every replica applies every write, and the leader alone cannot take 30,000 per second. The data itself must be split: **partitioning**, also called **sharding**.",
