        "answer": 1,
        "explanation": "Storage needs 5 ÷ 1 = 5 shards and writes need 30,000 ÷ 5,000 = 6. Both limits must hold, so the larger, 6, wins. Adding them (11) double-counts: each shard provides both storage and write capacity.",
