  {
    "title": "Split by date",
    "body": "The first idea is **range partitioning** by order date: January's orders on shard 1, February's on shard 2, and so on. Reports for one month read one shard. But every new order has today's date, so all 30,000 new writes per second go to the newest shard, six times what it can take, while the other five sit idle. This is a **hot partition**.",
