  {
    "title": "Split by a hash of the customer",
    "body": "With **hash partitioning** by `customer_id`, the key goes through a hash function (Level 3) and the hash picks the shard, so customers spread evenly: about 5,000 writes per second each. \"My orders\" includes the customer id, so it reads one shard. A query without the key, such as \"all orders placed today\", must ask all six shards and combine the answers: **scatter-gather**.",
