  {
    "title": "One seller, too many orders",
    "body": "A large business account places 20% of all orders: 0.2 × 30,000 = 6,000 writes per second for one `customer_id`. All of them hash to the same shard, which also serves its other customers, so it is overloaded: a **hot key**. More shards cannot help, because one key always goes to one shard. Splitting the key into 4 sub-keys, `seller42#0` to `seller42#3`, spreads it as about 1,500 writes per second each; reading that account's orders then reads 4 sub-keys.",
