  {
    "title": "Adding a seventh shard",
    "body": "With \"hash mod 6\", a key's shard is its hash's remainder when divided by 6. Adding a seventh shard changes the rule to \"mod 7\", and a key stays only if both remainders are the same, which happens for about 1 key in 7. So about 6 in 7, **86%** of all orders, would have to move to another shard, while the system keeps serving traffic.",
