  {
    "title": "A ring instead of mod",
    "body": "With **consistent hashing**, servers and keys are both placed on a ring of hash values, and each key belongs to the next server clockwise. A new server takes over only the keys between it and the server before it: about 1 ÷ 7 ≈ **14%** of keys. Every other key keeps its shard, so adding a server is a small, gradual move.",
