  {
    "title": "Many points per server",
    "body": "With one point per server, the gaps on the ring are uneven: one server can own a much larger slice than another, and a new server takes keys from only one neighbor. With **virtual nodes**, each server gets many points, for example 100, scattered around the ring. Each server's share comes out close to even, and a new server takes small slices from every other server. Each shard still keeps its own replicas and backups (SD 6).",
